# Tile card

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A Tile card shows one entity in a small, even tile: an icon, a name and the state written in words. Selecting the tile opens More info, or runs the action you set. It is the usual card for a light, a lock, a sensor or a person when a dashboard needs many entities at a glance.

This page owns the Home Assistant Tile card (`type: tile`) and its three parts. The controls that can sit on a tile are on [Card features (tile and area inline controls)](card-features.html). For many entities with long names, use an [Entities card](entities-card-and-entity-rows.html).

This page covers:

- `hui-tile-card`
- `ha-tile-icon`
- `ha-tile-info`
- `ha-tile-badge`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

A tile has three parts, left to right:

1. The icon, a round shape in the state colour. It can show a picture instead. A small badge can sit on its top right corner.
2. The information: the name on the first line and the state on the second, both on one line each.
3. Optional card features, below the information or beside it.

When the tile has an action, the whole tile is one button named by its name and its state. When it has card features, the card is a group named by its name.

